{"slug":"local-development","title":"Local Development","html":"<h1 id=\"local-development\">Local Development</h1>\n<p>Use <code>suprnova serve</code> for the normal development loop. It starts the Rust backend, Vite, and the TypeScript type watcher.</p>\n<h2 id=\"start-the-app\">Start the App</h2>\n<pre class=\"syntax-highlighting\"><code class=\"language-bash\"><span class=\"source shell bash\"><span class=\"meta function-call shell\"><span class=\"variable function shell\">suprnova</span></span><span class=\"meta function-call arguments shell\"> serve</span>\n</span></code></pre>\n<p>Expected ports:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Backend: <code>http://127.0.0.1:8765</code></li>\n<li>Frontend: <code>http://127.0.0.1:5765</code></li>\n</ul>\n<p>If you need to pin the ports explicitly:</p>\n<pre class=\"syntax-highlighting\"><code class=\"language-bash\"><span class=\"source shell bash\"><span class=\"meta function-call shell\"><span class=\"variable function shell\">suprnova</span></span><span class=\"meta function-call arguments shell\"> serve<span class=\"variable parameter option shell\"><span class=\"punctuation definition parameter shell\"> --</span>port</span> 8765<span class=\"variable parameter option shell\"><span class=\"punctuation definition parameter shell\"> --</span>frontend-port</span> 5765</span>\n</span></code></pre>\n<h2 id=\"separate-terminals\">Separate Terminals</h2>\n<p>Run the backend and frontend separately when you want more direct logs.</p>\n<pre class=\"syntax-highlighting\"><code class=\"language-bash\"><span class=\"source shell bash\"><span class=\"meta function-call shell\"><span class=\"variable function shell\">cargo</span></span><span class=\"meta function-call arguments shell\"> run<span class=\"variable parameter option shell\"><span class=\"punctuation definition parameter shell\"> --</span>bin</span> pulsar</span>\n</span></code></pre>\n<pre class=\"syntax-highlighting\"><code class=\"language-bash\"><span class=\"source shell bash\"><span class=\"meta function-call shell\"><span class=\"support function cd shell\">cd</span></span><span class=\"meta function-call arguments shell\"> frontend</span>\n<span class=\"meta function-call shell\"><span class=\"variable function shell\">bun</span></span><span class=\"meta function-call arguments shell\"> run dev<span class=\"keyword operator end-of-options shell\"> --</span></span><span class=\"meta function-call arguments shell\"> --host 127.0.0.1 --port 5765</span>\n</span></code></pre>\n<h2 id=\"build-generated-content\">Build Generated Content</h2>\n<p>Rebuild the manual after editing Markdown:</p>\n<pre class=\"syntax-highlighting\"><code class=\"language-bash\"><span class=\"source shell bash\"><span class=\"meta function-call shell\"><span class=\"variable function shell\">cargo</span></span><span class=\"meta function-call arguments shell\"> run<span class=\"variable parameter option shell\"><span class=\"punctuation definition parameter shell\"> --</span>bin</span> console<span class=\"keyword operator end-of-options shell\"> --</span></span><span class=\"meta function-call arguments shell\"> docs:build</span>\n</span></code></pre>\n<p>Seed starter articles:</p>\n<pre class=\"syntax-highlighting\"><code class=\"language-bash\"><span class=\"source shell bash\"><span class=\"meta function-call shell\"><span class=\"variable function shell\">cargo</span></span><span class=\"meta function-call arguments shell\"> run<span class=\"variable parameter option shell\"><span class=\"punctuation definition parameter shell\"> --</span>bin</span> console<span class=\"keyword operator end-of-options shell\"> --</span></span><span class=\"meta function-call arguments shell\"> articles:seed</span>\n</span></code></pre>\n<p>Promote a user for authoring:</p>\n<pre class=\"syntax-highlighting\"><code class=\"language-bash\"><span class=\"source shell bash\"><span class=\"meta function-call shell\"><span class=\"variable function shell\">cargo</span></span><span class=\"meta function-call arguments shell\"> run<span class=\"variable parameter option shell\"><span class=\"punctuation definition parameter shell\"> --</span>bin</span> console<span class=\"keyword operator end-of-options shell\"> --</span></span><span class=\"meta function-call arguments shell\"> users:promote --email user@example.com --role author</span>\n</span></code></pre>\n<h2 id=\"verification\">Verification</h2>\n<p>Run these before handing off a change:</p>\n<pre class=\"syntax-highlighting\"><code class=\"language-bash\"><span class=\"source shell bash\"><span class=\"meta function-call shell\"><span class=\"variable function shell\">cargo</span></span><span class=\"meta function-call arguments shell\"> test</span>\n<span class=\"meta function-call shell\"><span class=\"support function cd shell\">cd</span></span><span class=\"meta function-call arguments shell\"> frontend</span> <span class=\"keyword operator logical and shell\">&amp;&amp;</span> <span class=\"meta function-call shell\"><span class=\"variable function shell\">bun</span></span><span class=\"meta function-call arguments shell\"> run check</span> <span class=\"keyword operator logical and shell\">&amp;&amp;</span> <span class=\"meta function-call shell\"><span class=\"variable function shell\">bun</span></span><span class=\"meta function-call arguments shell\"> run build</span>\n</span></code></pre>\n<p>Use targeted tests while iterating:</p>\n<pre class=\"syntax-highlighting\"><code class=\"language-bash\"><span class=\"source shell bash\"><span class=\"meta function-call shell\"><span class=\"variable function shell\">cargo</span></span><span class=\"meta function-call arguments shell\"> test docs</span>\n<span class=\"meta function-call shell\"><span class=\"variable function shell\">cargo</span></span><span class=\"meta function-call arguments shell\"> test article_flows</span>\n</span></code></pre>\n<p>Continue with <a href=\"/docs/configuration\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Configuration</a>.</p>\n","excerpt":"Local Development Use suprnova serve for the normal development loop. It starts the Rust backend, Vite, and the TypeScript type watcher. Start the App suprnova serve Expected ports: Backend: http://127.0.0.1:8765 Frontend: http://127.0.0.1:...","headings":[{"level":1,"id":"local-development","title":"Local Development"},{"level":2,"id":"start-the-app","title":"Start the App"},{"level":2,"id":"separate-terminals","title":"Separate Terminals"},{"level":2,"id":"build-generated-content","title":"Build Generated Content"},{"level":2,"id":"verification","title":"Verification"}],"previous":"project-structure","next":"configuration"}